comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T04:07:31.782Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status census2922 and live pm search morning dispatcher plus open/in_progress lists and full canonical parent/history show pm-prrlce remains the broader owner; pm-wzmbvn is completed15-minute propagation work and pm-qawd is completed issue-permission work. This child owns only the newly observed automatic-origin alert and resolution gap."
  "2026-10-11T04:09:35.697Z","harness:codex","Regression proof: the new source-condition matrix fails on the shipped schedule-only workflow because a successful morning_dispatcher recovery cannot resolve its blocker (1failed/16passed). Repaired workflow includes only native schedule and explicitly declared workflow_dispatch/morning_dispatcher for automatic failure and success lifecycle; issue-trigger retry retains its own lifecycle, operator and unrelated events remain excluded. Real Bash bodies with a mock GitHub boundary prove both automatic origins supersede yesterday’s blocker and retain explicit origin diagnostics. Full linked workflow suite passes18tests. Actual accepted-but-unavailable publication report is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1437 with a corresponding PM-link comment; no republish or tag change."
  "2026-10-11T04:24:16.613Z","harness:codex","Full static verification exposed missing risk/confidence planning on this newly created owner. Supplied low risk/high confidence through the CLI; preserve the failed gate evidence and repeat the unchanged full gate after connected release repairs. This is a tracker planning correction, not a relaxed assurance policy."
  "2026-10-11T04:45:02.631Z","harness:codex","Final source verification:19linked workflow tests pass with source-condition and real Bash regressions; types/docs/skills, source quality, original SDK/CLI budgets, graph and record integrity, all336mutation controls and serialized9-package npm/npx/Bun/bunx acceptance pass. Earlier risk/planning and qualified transport failures remain documented; transport alone passes unchanged and graph gaps were repaired with typed edges. Reviewed delivery includes files/docs/test/history links and canonical external report GH1437. Hosted current-head checks/full review remain required after push; this source closure does not claim npm11is publicly available."
